reasoning_details.text:
Confirmed:
- ULTRAPLAN_QA_PRIMARY_SHARDS=7 works (undocumented in configuration.md's env list).
- `required_health:` empty → nil list, admitted with exit 0.

Now for the `required_health: []` → health command behavior, the chain is: RequestFromConfig.RequireHealth=nil → HealthRequest.Checks=[] → agentwrap CheckHealth runs all 8 default checks; RequiredChecks=[] → RequiredHealthFailure enforces every ran check. Let me verify this empirically with a stub `opencode` binary on PATH to be rigorous. I'll create a fake opencode that handles --version, run --help (with --format json text), providers list, models, but FAILS on "debug config" (simulating older CLI). Default config (3 checks) should pass health; cleared required_health should fail on runtime.config/runtime.runtime_paths.

Actually wait — even better: it also proves the inversion claim end-to-end. Let me do it.

Fake opencode script:
```bash
#!/bin/bash
case "$1" in
  --version) echo "opencode 1.0"; exit 0;;
  run) if [ "$2" == "--help" ]; then echo "usage: opencode run --format json"; exit 0; fi;;
  providers) echo "providers: anthropic auth available"; exit 0;;
  models) echo "models: anthropic/claude"; exit 0;;
  debug) echo "debug: unknown command" >&2; exit 1;;
esac
echo "unsupported" >&2; exit 1
```

Health request provider/model come from models.primary "provider/model" split → provider="provider", model="model". Provider check: `providers list provider` — my fake prints providers line regardless; contains "provider"? The needle is lowercased provider string = "provider". Output "providers: ..." contains "provider" → match → ready. Authentication check: needs line containing auth/login/key AND provider name... my output has no "auth"... wait I included "auth". If authentication check runs and providerLine lacks auth/login/key → Unknown status → required failure. Hmm that would make cleared-config fail via authentication too. Fine — any of these demonstrate the inversion. But careful: with DEFAULT config only runtime_available/structured_output/workdir run → all pass → health ok. With CLEARED config, extra checks run incl. debug probes → fail. Good contrast.

workdir check: req.WorkDir = workspace path exists → ready.

